---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Licensing"
  description="Licenses, attribution guidance, and exclusions for Aflora software and publication content."
>
  <header class="page-header">
    <p class="eyebrow">Licensing</p>
    <h1>Built to be studied, shared, and adapted.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Aflora separates software from publication content so each kind of work has
      a license designed for it.
    </p>
  </header>

  <article class="lesson-body">
    <h2>Software: MIT</h2>
    <p>
      Aflora's original source code, tests, build scripts, configuration, and
      technical documentation are licensed under the
      <a href="https://opensource.org/license/mit">MIT License</a>. The license
      permits use, modification, and distribution while requiring preservation
      of its copyright and license notice.
    </p>

    <h2>Publication content: CC BY 4.0</h2>
    <p>
      Unless a work says otherwise, original articles, newsletter issues, and
      educational illustrations are licensed under the
      <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">
        Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License
      </a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      You may share and adapt that material, including commercially, when you
      credit Lucca Emmanuel, link to the license, and identify your changes. A
      reasonable credit is: <q>“Title of work” by Lucca Emmanuel, from Aflora,
      licensed under CC BY 4.0.</q>
    </p>

    <h2>What is excluded</h2>
    <p>
      These grants do not cover the Aflora name or logo, branded social cards,
      third-party materials, cited works, or externally sourced data. Those
      elements remain subject to their source terms. The licenses grant no
      trademark rights and do not imply endorsement.
    </p>
    <p>
      The repository contains the complete
      <a href="https://github.com/luccae11235/grove/blob/main/LICENSING.md">
        path-level licensing guide
      </a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
